Dumpsters shall be screened in the manner described below:
(a) Screening shall be a minimum height of six feet;
(b) All four sides of the dumpster shall be screened;
(c) The screen should incorporate access to the dumpster by using a wood fence or other opaque device to serve as a gate;
(d) Screening materials can be any combination of evergreen plantings, wood, or masonry material.
